{
  "date": "2026-11-20",
  "baseline": "9bf7d80 plus existing workspace changes (including the same long-ASCII scan and the correction for densely compressed v2 frames in both builds). Only the direct 26-byte timestamp parser and the column-local previous-value lookup differ. To build the baseline from the candidate, remove the new 26-byte branch at the start of tryParseAsciiDateTime, and replace _decodeObjectColumn through the end of _sameTemporalBytes with _decodeObjectColumn from 9bf7d80. Keep the rest of the sources and the native DLL identical.",
  "environment": "Dart 3.14.0 AOT, Windows x64, local SQL Server via ODBC, balancedServer. Both binaries loaded the same release DLL (SHA-256 533E6E5C765559C43850255A89341D8D9054B9DA5D91A0FDF72662628811BD36).",
  "timezone": "Central Brazilian Standard Time",
  "reproduction": [
    "Set ODBC_TEST_DSN to a SQL Server test connection and ODBC_FAST_NATIVE_LIBRARY to the absolute path of the release odbc_engine.dll.",
    "In each revision, using identical benchmarks/hot_timestamp_read.dart, run dart compile exe --packages=.dart_tool/package_config.json benchmarks/hot_timestamp_read.dart -o .tmp/ts-final-REVISION.exe (substitute before or after).",
    "Compile benchmarks/large_result_live.dart the same way on each revision for the integer and long-text control. Run before, after, after and before in sequence. For each build run the timestamp executable with --clustered first, then without arguments, followed by the control executable. Each invocation writes JSON containing microseconds per call."
  ],
  "workload": "Read-only ordered SELECT, two datetime2(6) columns, second is NULL every seventh row. For each size: unique timestamp each row or the same timestamp for 64 rows. All cells verified after timing. API calls include SQL, transfer and decoding. Parser calls reuse a frame fetched before timing in the requested encoding.",
  "sampling": "Three warmups then nine samples per path per process, rotating path order. Two processes per build and workload yield 18 samples per cell. Distribution summaries use pooled median and inclusive quartiles in microseconds. Percent denotes reduction in median elapsed time relative to baseline. Short API calls are sensitive to Windows timer scheduling.",
  "neighbor_control": "The text group is the unchanged large_result_live.dart workload: 512 rows of two integers, optionally with 2048 ASCII characters and NULL every seventh row. Four warmups and 21 samples per process (42 total per build). Checked timings also include verifying all values.",
  "compression_regression": "Before the correctness fix both decoders compared rows with compressed byte size. A read-only query returned 512 valid rows in 252 bytes; the retained deterministic regression uses 512 null markers in a 41-byte zstd frame. The fix checks expanded column lengths before allocating output. The prior failing implementation cannot supply a dense-compressed performance baseline.",
  "interpretation": "The largest end-to-end improvement was for repeated temporal values in the typed columnar API. The 512-row unique row API median increased from 23.02 to 24.22 ms with overlapping IQRs (20.72\u201324.46 vs 18.06\u201326.31 ms), despite a reduction in parser time. No end-to-end gain is established at one row. Integer and text controls and FFI timings are not attributed to the timestamp changes. Protocol and related suites: 345 passed.",
  "validation": [
    "dart analyze --fatal-infos lib/infrastructure/native/protocol/binary_protocol_columnar.dart lib/infrastructure/native/protocol/protocol_ascii_parse.dart test/infrastructure/native/protocol/binary_protocol_test.dart test/infrastructure/native/protocol/timestamp_decode_test.dart test/infrastructure/native/protocol/columnar_v2_zstd_golden_test.dart benchmarks/hot_timestamp_read.dart",
    "dart test test/infrastructure/native/protocol test/infrastructure/native/columnar_decompress_ffi_test.dart test/infrastructure/native/async_connection/binary_protocol_parser_test.dart test/infrastructure/repositories/runners/stream_columnar_runner_test.dart test/domain/helpers/typed_columnar_materialization_test.dart test/performance/stream_columnar_roundtrip_test.dart --reporter expanded"
  ],
